                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                        "entry_id": "a0e45bc1-3a04-3e93-9d3b-1e708c27ea9a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The state of being precocious."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "81452096-3818-49f8-a7dd-57bd08c17728",
                                "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                                "text": "1817 William Wirt, Sketches of the Life and Character of Patrick Henry, New York: M'elrath, Bangs & Co., 1834, Section I, pp. 23-4, https://books.google.ca/books?id=5vE5AAAAcAAJ&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\nI cannot learn that he gave in his youth, any evidence of that precocity which sometimes distinguishes uncommon genius."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02ff81bc-0b83-47ab-8d63-dfe9ae8a3243",
                                "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                                "text": "By the side of many tall and bouncing young ladies in the establishment, Rebecca Sharp looked like a child. But she had the dismal precocity of poverty."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "92a8cfd8-e500-4f51-a0bf-533db721f8b7",
                                "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                                "text": "It was as if his precocity of crookedness (and every vulgar villain is precocious) had for once deceived him, and the man he had sought to entrap as a simpleton had, through his very simplicity, ignominiously baffled him."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c21e99cd-d266-46ce-b940-a6eb9d3b4433",
                                "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                                "text": "1946, Arnold J. Toynbee, A Study of History, Abridgement of Volumes I-VI by D.C. Somervell, Oxford University Press, Chapter XII, p. 242, https://books.google.ca/books?id=IbJ-31LPvyoC&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false\nAnna Comnena, the Byzantine princess turned historian, sees our eleventh-century forebears in just this light, as appears in the mixture of horror with contempt which is her reaction to the mechanical ingenuity of the Crusaders' cross-bow, a Western novelty of her day which—with the characteristic precocity of lethal inventions—preceded by several centuries the invention of clockwork […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "932b62ee-7814-4e80-8e31-6216bd45242e",
                                "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                                "text": "How can we explain the relative precocity in political studies that the Greeks demonstrated in contrast to the backwardness of other early peoples?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a45e36e-951c-4982-ac5c-d81e866e8016",
                                "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                                "text": "Short stature persists into adult life but puberty is usually normal, although sexual precocity has been seen […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3bd5637-8aac-4860-a7a9-47ed2ec38a45",
                                "sense_id": "0dc4277c-42aa-37da-8606-44f883c5ea94",
                                "text": "2024 (October 20th) The Simpsons season 36 episode 3 \"Desperately Seeking Lisa\"\nYes, she's truly a special young person, just brimming with precocity. In fact, I was thinking she might be a good fit for the Horace Frick Academy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
